     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't resolve either concern.\n\n- **Safety:** 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum dose of 200 mg. It could seriously harm the patient. Confirming the number doesn't make it safe.\n- **Authority:** You've told me you're not a clinician. A confirmation from you isn't a prescriber's verification.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the treating prescriber to review the intended dose. If it was a typo, they can give me the corrected order, such as 100 mg once daily.\n- If a prescriber really intends a dose above the labeled maximum, which would be highly unusual, they should enter it themselves. It would need pharmacy review and documented clinical justification.\n- If this order came from somewhere else, such as a note or a message, flag it to the pharmacy or the care team so the error can be traced.\n\nI can enter a corrected order once a prescriber confirms the intended dose."
      }
     ],
